<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This example illustrates how the product <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> can be partitioned into disjoint matrix components, forming a support basis that enables structured approximation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Bounded Entry</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now establish an upper bound on the entries of the matrix <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(s)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to the contribution from the small entries of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows us to apply polynomial approximation techniques with controlled error. We generalize the bounded-entry result from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> to arbitrary thresholds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.8</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded entry, an improved version of Lemma 3.3 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition B.4. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, where</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\left(s\right)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}0&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{if}~\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\not=0\\
\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>otherwise</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\left(s\right)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}0&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{if}~\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\not=0\\
\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for a given threshold <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq T^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq T^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|A^{\left(s\right)}\right\|_{\infty}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|A^{\left(s\right)}\right\|_{\infty}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|A^{\left(s\right)}_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|A^{\left(s\right)}_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|\sum_{l=1}^{d}Q^{\left(s\right)}_{i,l}K^{\left(s\right)}_{j,l}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|\sum_{l=1}^{d}Q^{\left(s\right)}_{i,l}K^{\left(s\right)}_{j,l}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}\left|\max_{i\in[n]}Q^{\left(s\right)}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\left|\max_{j\in[n]}K^{\left(s\right)}_{j,l}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}\left|\max_{i\in[n]}Q^{\left(s\right)}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\left|\max_{j\in[n]}K^{\left(s\right)}_{j,l}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}T^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}T^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~dT^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~dT^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, the second step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(s\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(s\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition B.4. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>), the third step follows from the triangle inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), and the fourth step follows from Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Running Time and Sparsity Analysis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we analyze the sparsity and computational cost associated with the matrix <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which captures the contribution from the large entries of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to exactly compute the part of the attention computation involving <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate the part involving <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(s)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it is important to know the time complexity for constructing <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> and its sparsity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.9</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the query and the key matrices <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>
and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)},A^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)},A^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition B.4. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">it takes </span><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> time to compute </span><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 1.<span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that by Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition B.4. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\left(L\right)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}\left(QK^{\top}\right)_{i,j}&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{if}~\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\not=0\\
0&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>otherwise</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\left(L\right)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}\left(QK^{\top}\right)_{i,j}&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{if}~\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\not=0\\
0&amp;\quad\quad\mathrm{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(i,j\right)\notin\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(i,j\right)\notin\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\left(L\right)}_{i,j}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\left(L\right)}_{i,j}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, it suffices to consider the case when</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that by Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|,\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|\leq Cn^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|,\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|\leq Cn^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">for a fixed constant <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|+\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact J.1. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.1</span></a>, the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), the third step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and the last step follows from <math id="A2.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2.<span id="A2.SS4.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of this part is similar to that of <span id="A2.SS4.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">It also suffices to only consider the case when</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), we have that</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">computing <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">computing <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">computing <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A2.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, because of Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex54" title="In Proof. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we need to compute <math id="A2.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> numbers of entries of <math id="A2.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for each <math id="A2.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}=\sum_{k\in[d]}\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\right)_{i,k}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}_{k,j}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}=\sum_{k\in[d]}\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\right)_{i,k}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}_{k,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">which takes <math id="A2.SS4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, in total, it takes <math id="A2.SS4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> times to compute <math id="A2.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the time complexity of computing</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(QK^{\top}\right)_{i,j}=\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(QK^{\top}\right)_{i,j}=\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A2.SS4.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(i,j\right)\in\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(L\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(L\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(n^{2\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)+O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>(Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now formalize the task of computing <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AV</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\exp(QK^{\top}/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\exp(QK^{\top}/d)</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix. This operation is closely related to a classical technique in statistics known as <em id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation (KDE)</em>. In Gaussian KDE, the goal is to estimate a density function by averaging Gaussian kernels centered at given data points. Given data points <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and a query point <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the classical Gaussian KDE estimate is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{f}(q)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\exp\left(-\frac{\|q-x_{j}\|_{2}^{2}}{2h^{2}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{f}(q)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\exp\left(-\frac{\|q-x_{j}\|_{2}^{2}}{2h^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the Gaussian kernel can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(-\frac{\|q-k\|_{2}^{2}}{2h^{2}}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(-\frac{\|q-k\|_{2}^{2}}{2h^{2}}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(-\frac{\|q\|_{2}^{2}+\|k\|_{2}^{2}-2\langle q,k\rangle}{2h^{2}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(-\frac{\|q\|_{2}^{2}+\|k\|_{2}^{2}-2\langle q,k\rangle}{2h^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the attention computation problem focus primarily on</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(\frac{\langle q,k\rangle}{h^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(\frac{\langle q,k\rangle}{h^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The matrix product <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AV</annotation></semantics></math> can therefore be interpreted as a <em id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">batch</em> version of Gaussian KDE, where each row of <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AV</annotation></semantics></math> aggregates value vectors <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{*,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{*,k}</annotation></semantics></math> weighted by the similarity between query <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i,*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i,*}</annotation></semantics></math> and key <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{j,*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{j,*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This motivates the name <em id="A2.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation</em>, as it generalizes Gaussian KDE to the matrix setting. We now formally define the problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.10</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>((Batch) Gaussian kernel density estimation)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, key <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and value <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1.1 ((𝑄,𝐾)-softmax-attention matrix). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>. The goal of the (batch) Gaussian kernel density estimation is to output <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying, for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mathsf{S}-AV\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mathsf{S}-AV\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Having defined the (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation problem, we now show how our algorithm can approximate <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AV</annotation></semantics></math> efficiently by leveraging the support basis decomposition. Specifically, we use polynomial approximation for the component <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(s)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which contains only small entries and is thus suitable for Chebyshev expansion, and we compute the remaining part <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly, exploiting its sparsity. The following lemma guarantees the correctness and efficiency of this approach by bounding the approximation error and analyzing the overall runtime.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> In this algorithm, we approximate the (batch) Gaussian kernel density estimation: given the query, key, and value matrices <math id="alg3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the goal is to output <math id="alg3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}V</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="alg3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="alg3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon,r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon,r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of the <math id="alg3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="alg3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">procedure</span> <span id="alg3.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GaussianKDE</span>(<math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},n,d,\epsilon,T=o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d},n,d,\epsilon,T=o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}\leftarrow\textsc{Split}(Q,T),\textsc{Split}(K,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Split</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Split</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}\leftarrow\textsc{Split}(Q,T),\textsc{Split}(K,T)</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              Explicitly compute <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}\leftarrow\textsc{Polynomial}(Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(s\right)},\epsilon_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Polynomial</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}\leftarrow\textsc{Polynomial}(Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(s\right)},\epsilon_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> To approximate <math id="alg3.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Get <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\leftarrow U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\leftarrow U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Get <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}\leftarrow\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}\leftarrow\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}+C_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}+C_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. 

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">procedure</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.11</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, key <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and value <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1.1 ((𝑄,𝐾)-softmax-attention matrix). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>. Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> for any arbitrary <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can solve the (Batch) Gaussian kernel density estimation (Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Definition B.10 ((Batch) Gaussian kernel density estimation). ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a>) by outputting <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mathsf{S}-AV\right\|_{\infty}&lt;n\epsilon_{0}\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mathsf{S}-AV\right\|_{\infty}&lt;n\epsilon_{0}\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of correctness.<span id="A2.SS5.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle AV=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle AV=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(A^{\left(s\right)}+A^{\left(L\right)}\right)/d\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(A^{\left(s\right)}+A^{\left(L\right)}\right)/d\right)V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)V+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)V-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}V," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)V+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)V-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of the <math id="A2.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix (see Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1.1 ((𝑄,𝐾)-softmax-attention matrix). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), the second step follows from Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, and the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact B.2. ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 (Bounded entry, an improved version of Lemma 3.3 in []). ‣ B.3 Bounded Entry ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq T^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq T^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some threshold <math id="A2.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By setting the threshold <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> to be equal to <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can see that this satisfies the assumption of using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> and Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Therefore, using Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)-U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)-U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any arbitrary <math id="A2.SS5.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we output</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{S}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{S}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~C_{1}+C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~C_{1}+C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)+\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)+\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)V-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}V," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)V-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the output (Line <a href="#alg3.l7" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) of Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and the second step follows from updates <math id="A2.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\leftarrow U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\leftarrow U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Line <a href="#alg3.l5" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and <math id="A2.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}\leftarrow\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}\leftarrow\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Line <a href="#alg3.l6" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, combining Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex68" title="In Proof. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex71" title="In Proof. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mathsf{S}-AV\right\|_{\infty}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mathsf{S}-AV\right\|_{\infty}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}V-\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)V\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}V-\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)V\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}-\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)\right)V\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}-\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)\right)V\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~n\left\|U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}-\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty}\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~n\left\|U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}-\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty}\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~n\epsilon_{0}\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~n\epsilon_{0}\left\|V\right\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from combining Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex71" title="In Proof. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex68" title="In Proof. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), the second step follows from the distributive law, the third step follows from the definition of the <math id="A2.SS5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, and the fourth step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of the running time.<span id="A2.SS5.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Line <a href="#alg3.l2" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we need to check each entry of <math id="A2.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> finding the ones greater than the threshold <math id="A2.SS5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, which takes <math id="A2.SS5.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nd)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Line <a href="#alg3.l3" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we compute <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. By <span id="A2.SS5.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma B.9. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>, we know that it takes <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time to compute <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Line <a href="#alg3.l4" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we construct <math id="A2.SS5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, which by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> takes <math id="A2.SS5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nr)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Line <a href="#alg3.l5" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, it takes <math id="A2.SS5.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nrd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nrd)</annotation></semantics></math> time to compute <math id="A2.SS5.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{2}^{\top}V\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{2}^{\top}V\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and takes <math id="A2.SS5.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nrd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nrd)</annotation></semantics></math> time to compute <math id="A2.SS5.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}\left(U_{2}^{\top}V\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Line <a href="#alg3.l6" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, it takes <math id="A2.SS5.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{1+\alpha}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{1+\alpha}d)</annotation></semantics></math> time to compute <math id="A2.SS5.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V</annotation></semantics></math> as by <span id="A2.SS5.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma B.9. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>, we know that <math id="A2.SS5.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> which implies <math id="A2.SS5.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">In total, it takes <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{1+\alpha}d+nrd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{1+\alpha}d+nrd)</annotation></semantics></math> time. By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, we know that <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nr)=n^{1+o(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nr)=n^{1+o(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O(n^{1+\alpha}d+nrd)=O(n^{1+\alpha}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O(n^{1+\alpha}d+nrd)=O(n^{1+\alpha}d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Relationship Between the Attention Matrix and the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we cite a lemma from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> stating that if we can have the relative error between the <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and the approximate <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can find the relative error between <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diag(A{\bf 1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diag(A{\bf 1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diag(\widetilde{A}{\bf 1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diag(\widetilde{A}{\bf 1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. In Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 The Error Bound for the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, we get the relative error between <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diag(A{\bf 1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diag(A{\bf 1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\diag(\widetilde{A}{\bf 1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\diag(\widetilde{A}{\bf 1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> by finding the relative error between <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. In Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Main Result ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we combine these relative errors with our result on the (batch) Gaussian kernel density estimation (Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma B.11. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>) to construct an <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity time algorithm to approximate the attention computation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Relationship Between the Attention Matrix and the Normalization Matrix</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We cite Lemma 3.5 from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> which states that if we can get <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot D_{i,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot D_{i,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 3.5 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be any matrix whose entries are all positive and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{A}\in(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{A}\in(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math> be any parameter. Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be any matrix such that, for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in[n]\times[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in[n]\times[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the matrices <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D,\widetilde{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D,\widetilde{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\mathrm{diag}(A\mathbf{1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\mathrm{diag}(A\mathbf{1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{D}=\mathrm{diag}(\widetilde{A}\mathbf{1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{D}=\mathrm{diag}(\widetilde{A}\mathbf{1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot D_{i,i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot D_{i,i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-\sum_{j=1}^{n}A_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\sum_{j=1}^{n}\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-\sum_{j=1}^{n}A_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{A}A_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{A}A_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\epsilon_{A}\cdot D_{i,i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\epsilon_{A}\cdot D_{i,i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\mathrm{diag}(A\mathbf{1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\mathrm{diag}(A\mathbf{1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{D}=\mathrm{diag}(\widetilde{A}\mathbf{1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{D}=\mathrm{diag}(\widetilde{A}\mathbf{1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, the second step follows from the triangle inequality (Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), the third step follows from the assumption in the lemma statement <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\mathrm{diag}(A\mathbf{1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\mathrm{diag}(A\mathbf{1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>The Error Bound for the Normalization Matrix</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we prove <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|\leq\epsilon_{A}\cdot A_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> so that by the logic of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Lemma 3.5 in []). ‣ C.1 Relationship Between the Attention Matrix and the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we can get <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon\cdot D_{i,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon\cdot D_{i,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the query <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and the key <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1.1 ((𝑄,𝐾)-softmax-attention matrix). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>. Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(s\right)}\left(K^{\left(s\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> for any arbitrary <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}=U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}=U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{D}:=\diag\left(\widetilde{A}{\bf 1}_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{D}:=\diag\left(\widetilde{A}{\bf 1}_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:=\diag\left(A{\bf 1}_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=\diag\left(A{\bf 1}_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can show that for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon\cdot D_{i,i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon\cdot D_{i,i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, for all <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{A}_{i,j}-A_{i,j}\right|=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)_{i,j}-\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)_{i,j}-\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}-U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}-\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)+{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}-U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}-\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)+{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)-U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)-U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\epsilon\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)\right)_{i,j}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\epsilon\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)\right)_{i,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex68" title="In Proof. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) for detail) and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}=U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}=U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (see from the lemma statement) and the last step follows from Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Lemma 3.5 in []). ‣ C.1 Relationship Between the Attention Matrix and the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we have for all <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon\cdot D_{i,i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}-D_{i,i}\right|\leq\epsilon\cdot D_{i,i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Main Result</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now state our main theoretical result for the single-threshold support basis framework. Building on Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma B.11. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ C.2 The Error Bound for the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, we show that the entire attention computation <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{-1}AV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{-1}AV</annotation></semantics></math> can be approximated in <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity time with a relative error guarantee. Our approach combines two key components: a polynomial approximation for the bounded portion of the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix, and an explicit computation for the sparse, large entries. Together, these enable us to construct an approximate attention output <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|P-D^{-1}AV\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|P-D^{-1}AV\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any accuracy <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The following theorem formalizes this guarantee and provides the corresponding runtime bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the query <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, key <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and value <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1.1 ((𝑄,𝐾)-softmax-attention matrix). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(L\right)},Q^{\left(s\right)},K^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(s\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition B.3. ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.
Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can solve the approximate attention computation (Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Definition 1.3 (The approximate attention computation). ‣ 1.2 Background ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a>) by outputting <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|P-D^{-1}AV\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|P-D^{-1}AV\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon\left\|V\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{1+\alpha}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{1+\alpha}d)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of correctness.<span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|D^{-1}AV-\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|D^{-1}AV-\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|D^{-1}AV-D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V+D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|D^{-1}AV-D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V+D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|D^{-1}AV-D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}+\left\|D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|D^{-1}AV-D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}+\left\|D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V\right\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, we have for each <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in[n]\times[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in[n]\times[d]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|(\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V)_{i,j}\right|=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|(\widetilde{D}^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V)_{i,j}\right|=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left(\widetilde{D}^{-1}_{i,i}-D^{-1}_{i,i}\right)\cdot\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\cdot V_{l,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left(\widetilde{D}^{-1}_{i,i}-D^{-1}_{i,i}\right)\cdot\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\cdot V_{l,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|\widetilde{D}^{-1}_{i,i}-D^{-1}_{i,i}\right|\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|\widetilde{D}^{-1}_{i,i}-D^{-1}_{i,i}\right|\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|\frac{D_{i,i}-\widetilde{D}_{i,i}}{D_{i,i}\widetilde{D}_{i,i}}\right|\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|\frac{D_{i,i}-\widetilde{D}_{i,i}}{D_{i,i}\widetilde{D}_{i,i}}\right|\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex96.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex98.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the triangle inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), the fourth step follows from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ C.2 The Error Bound for the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{D_{i,i}-\widetilde{D}_{i,i}}{D_{i,i}}\right|\leq\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{D_{i,i}-\widetilde{D}_{i,i}}{D_{i,i}}\right|\leq\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">the fifth step follows from <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}_{i,l}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}_{i,l}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\right|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}\widetilde{D}_{i,i}^{-1}\widetilde{A}_{i,l}\right|=1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\diag(A{\bf 1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\diag(A{\bf 1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Also, for each <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in[n]\times[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in[n]\times[d]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|(D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-D^{-1}AV)_{i,j}\right|=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|(D^{-1}\widetilde{A}V-D^{-1}AV)_{i,j}\right|=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex100.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}D^{-1}_{i,i}(\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l})\cdot V_{l,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\sum_{l=1}^{n}D^{-1}_{i,i}(\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l})\cdot V_{l,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex101.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|D^{-1}_{i,i}\right|\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}\left|D^{-1}_{i,i}\right|\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex102.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}D^{-1}_{i,i}\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}D^{-1}_{i,i}\cdot|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l}|\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex103.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}D^{-1}_{i,i}\cdot\epsilon A_{i,l}\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{n}D^{-1}_{i,i}\cdot\epsilon A_{i,l}\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from triangle inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), the third step follows from <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{-1}_{i,i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{-1}_{i,i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the fourth step follows from <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l}|\leq\epsilon\cdot A_{i,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widetilde{A}_{i,l}-A_{i,l}|\leq\epsilon\cdot A_{i,l}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ C.2 The Error Bound for the Normalization Matrix ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), and the last step follows from definition of <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Running time.<span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar as the proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma B.11. ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>, Line <a href="#alg1.l4" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to Line <a href="#alg1.l8" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> takes <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{1+\alpha}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{1+\alpha}d)</annotation></semantics></math> time, Line <a href="#alg1.l9" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> to Line <a href="#alg1.l10" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> take <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{1+\alpha}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{1+\alpha}d)</annotation></semantics></math> time, and computing <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{-1}(C_{1}+C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{-1}(C_{1}+C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nd)</annotation></semantics></math> time (as <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we justify the sparsity assumption used in our single-threshold support basis decomposition by introducing a natural probabilistic model: the sub-Gaussian distribution. Empirically, the entries of the query and key matrices in large language models tend to concentrate near zero and exhibit light tails—properties well captured by sub-Gaussian random variables. Under this assumption, we show that the number of “large” entries in <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (those exceeding a chosen threshold) is small with high probability. This validates our decomposition strategy and ensures that the matrix <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> remains sparse. We also analyze the expected number of large entries and their contribution to the <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix, supporting the theoretical guarantees presented in Appendices <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> and <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 The Definition of Sub-Gaussian Distribution ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, we present the formal definition of a sub-Gaussian distribution. In Appendix <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 The Expected Number of Large Entries ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we assume that the entries of the query matrix <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and the key matrix <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> follow sub-Gaussian distributions and show that the expected number of entries exceeding any threshold <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. In Appendix <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 The Number of Non-Zero Entries ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, we prove that the number of non-zero entries in <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with high probability. Finally, in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Approximating the Attention Computation Under the Sub-Gaussian Assumption ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, we combine this sparsity result with our main result on attention optimization (Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem C.3. ‣ C.3 Main Result ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>) to show that, with high probability, the attention computation can be approximated in sub-quadratic time. Thus, we finally can formally justify that the <math id="A4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity time <math id="A4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem C.3. ‣ C.3 Main Result ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> is truly sub-quadratic in <math id="A4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>The Definition of Sub-Gaussian Distribution</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To formally analyze the statistical properties of the query and key matrices, we begin by introducing the notion of a sub-Gaussian distribution. Sub-Gaussian random variables exhibit tail behavior similar to or lighter than that of a Gaussian, making them a natural model for the entries of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in practice. This assumption enables us to rigorously bound the probability and expected number of large entries, which is essential for proving sparsity and deriving sub-quadratic algorithms.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proposition 2.5.2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A random variable <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be sub-Gaussian with variance <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathrm{subG}(\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>subG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathrm{subG}(\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, if</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[|X|\geq t\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{\sigma^{2}}\right)\quad\text{for all }t\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[|X|\geq t\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{\sigma^{2}}\right)\quad\text{for all }t\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>The Expected Number of Large Entries</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the sub-Gaussian assumption, we can now quantify how many entries in the query and key matrices exceed a given threshold. Specifically, the following lemma shows that the expected number of such large entries decays exponentially with the threshold. This result supports our sparsity assumption for <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and plays a key role in bounding the size of the matrix <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> used in our support basis decomposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expected Number of Large Entries Under Sub-Gaussianity)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be random matrices whose entries are independent and sub-Gaussian with variance proxies <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Q}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Q}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{K}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{K}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{V}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{V}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, which implies that for all <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[|Q_{i,j}|\geq t\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[|Q_{i,j}|\geq t\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and similarly for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a threshold. Define <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(L)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,j}&amp;\text{if }|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(L)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,j}&amp;\text{if }|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and similarly for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{(L)},V^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{(L)},V^{(L)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for all <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(L)}\in\{Q^{(L)},K^{(L)},V^{(L)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(L)}\in\{Q^{(L)},K^{(L)},V^{(L)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{M}\in\{\sigma_{Q},\sigma_{K},\sigma_{V}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{M}\in\{\sigma_{Q},\sigma_{K},\sigma_{V}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}(M^{(L)})\right|\right]\leq 2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{M}^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}(M^{(L)})\right|\right]\leq 2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{M}^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a matrix <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\{Q,K,V\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\{Q,K,V\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n],j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n],j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the indicator variable</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{i,j}:=\mathbb{I}\left[|M_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}:=\mathbb{I}\left[|M_{i,j}|&gt;T\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}(M^{(L)})\right|=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{d}X_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}(M^{(L)})\right|=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{d}X_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, taking expectation and using linearity, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(M^{(L)}\right)\right|\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(M^{(L)}\right)\right|\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex110.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\Pr\left[|M_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\Pr\left[|M_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{M}^{2}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{M}^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last step follows from the sub-Gaussian tail bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>The Number of Non-Zero Entries</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we strengthen the result of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Expected Number of Large Entries Under Sub-Gaussianity). ‣ D.2 The Expected Number of Large Entries ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> by moving from an expectation bound to a high-probability guarantee. Specifically, we show that with high probability, the number of large entries in the query and key matrices is at most <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The bound of the number of non-zero entries of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{(L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{(L)}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be random matrices with independent entries such that each <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i,j},K_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i,j},K_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian with variance proxies <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Q}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Q}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{K}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{K}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. For a constant <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and a threshold <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\sqrt{c\log n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\sqrt{c\log n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the large-entry matrices:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(L)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,j}&amp;\text{if }|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\quad K^{(L)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}K_{i,j}&amp;\text{if }|K_{i,j}|&gt;T,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(L)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,j}&amp;\text{if }|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\quad K^{(L)}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}K_{i,j}&amp;\text{if }|K_{i,j}|&gt;T,\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for all <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\left(L\right)}\in\{Q^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(L\right)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\left(L\right)}\in\{Q^{\left(L\right)},K^{\left(L\right)}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(M^{(L)}\right)\right|&gt;n^{\alpha}\right]\leq\exp\left(-\Omega(n^{\alpha})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(M^{(L)}\right)\right|&gt;n^{\alpha}\right]\leq\exp\left(-\Omega(n^{\alpha})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since each <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i,j}\in\mathrm{subG}(\sigma_{Q}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>subG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i,j}\in\mathrm{subG}(\sigma_{Q}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly for <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X=\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{(L)}\right)\right|=\sum_{i,j}\mathbb{I}\left[|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{(L)}\right)\right|=\sum_{i,j}\mathbb{I}\left[|Q_{i,j}|&gt;T\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We note that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of independent entries.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (Expected Number of Large Entries Under Sub-Gaussianity). ‣ D.2 The Expected Number of Large Entries ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex115.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{T^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex116.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{c\log n}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\exp\left(-\frac{c\log n}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex117.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\left(e^{\log n}\right)^{-\frac{c}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2nd\cdot\left(e^{\log n}\right)^{-\frac{c}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~2nd\cdot n^{-c/\sigma_{Q}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2nd\cdot n^{-c/\sigma_{Q}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~o(n^{\alpha})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~o(n^{\alpha}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last step follows from <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,\sigma_{Q}^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,\sigma_{Q}^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=O(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=O(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by a multiplicative Chernoff bound (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact J.5 (Multiplicative Chernoff Bound). ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.5</span></a>), for any <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[X&gt;(1+\delta)\mathbb{E}[X]\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}\cdot\mathbb{E}[X]}{3}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[X&gt;(1+\delta)\mathbb{E}[X]\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}\cdot\mathbb{E}[X]}{3}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, for large enough <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\alpha}&gt;(1+\delta)\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\alpha}&gt;(1+\delta)\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{(L)}\right)\right|&gt;n^{\alpha}\right]\leq\exp\left(-\Omega(n^{\alpha})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(Q^{(L)}\right)\right|&gt;n^{\alpha}\right]\leq\exp\left(-\Omega(n^{\alpha})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and likewise for <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(K^{(L)}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(K^{(L)}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Approximating the Attention Computation Under the Sub-Gaussian Assumption</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we combine the sparsity guarantees established in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (The bound of the number of non-zero entries of 𝑄^(𝐿) and 𝐾^(𝐿)). ‣ D.3 The Number of Non-Zero Entries ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> with our main result on attention approximation (Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem C.3. ‣ C.3 Main Result ‣ Appendix C ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>). The following theorem shows that, under the sub-Gaussian assumption, our algorithm approximates the attention computation and runs in sub-quadratic time with high probability. This provides a rigorous justification for the practical efficiency of our method and demonstrates that strong runtime guarantees can be achieved without requiring the bounded entry assumption, <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&lt;o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&lt;o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Main Theorem Under Sub-Gaussian Assumption)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be random matrices whose entries are independent and sub-Gaussian with variance proxies <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{Q}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{Q}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{K}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{K}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{V}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{V}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, which implies that for all <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[|Q_{i,j}|\geq t\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[|Q_{i,j}|\geq t\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{\sigma_{Q}^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and similarly for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fix a threshold <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\sqrt{c\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\sqrt{c\log n}</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math> be a target accuracy parameter. Then, with probability at least <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\exp(-\Omega(n^{\alpha}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp(-\Omega(n^{\alpha}))</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the output <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> from Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|P-D^{-1}AV\right\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|P-D^{-1}AV\right\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon\cdot\|V\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=\exp(QK^{\top}/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=\exp(QK^{\top}/d)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:=\mathrm{diag}(A\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=\mathrm{diag}(A\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, the runtime of the algorithm is</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{1+\alpha}d)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{1+\alpha}d).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (The bound of the number of non-zero entries of 𝑄^(𝐿) and 𝐾^(𝐿)). ‣ D.3 The Number of Non-Zero Entries ‣ Appendix D ATTENTION OPTIMIZATION UNDER THE SUB-GAUSSIAN DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, we have with probability <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\exp\left(-\Omega(n^{\alpha})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp\left(-\Omega(n^{\alpha})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(M^{(L)}\right)\right|\leq n^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(M^{(L)}\right)\right|\leq n^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma B.9. ‣ B.4 Running Time and Sparsity Analysis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{(L)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{(L)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">it takes <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time to compute <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{(L)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mathrm{supp}\left(A^{(L)}\right)\right|=O\left(n^{1+\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, computing <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right)V</annotation></semantics></math> (Line <a href="#alg3.l6" title="In Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ B.5 (Batch) Gaussian Kernel Density Estimation ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right){\bf 1}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}\right){\bf 1}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (Line <a href="#alg1.l7" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Conquer: Approximate the attention in 𝐴^(𝐿) sparsity time. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) take <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(n^{1+\alpha}d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> time.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>GENERALIZATION TO MULTI-LAYER TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that from Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 1.2 (The exact attention computation). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> we define the single-layer attention computation as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D^{-1}AV=D^{-1}\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)V." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D^{-1}AV=D^{-1}\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)V.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In transformer architectures, this only denotes one single layer of the forward propagation. Without loss of generality, we can suppose this is the <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer: the query matrix is defined as <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=X_{\beta}W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=X_{\beta}W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the key matrix is defined as <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=X_{\beta}W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=X_{\beta}W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the value matrix is defined as <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=X_{\beta}W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=X_{\beta}W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\beta}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input for the <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer and <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> are the weight matrices for the query, key, and value respectively. When attempting to optimize the <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer forward propagation, we can exactly compute the matrices <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(nd^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(nd^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> time, which is already sub-quadratic in <math id="A5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer can be formulated as the following recursive relation:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{\beta+1}\leftarrow D^{-1}\exp(X_{\beta}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}X_{\beta}^{\top})X_{\beta}W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{\beta+1}\leftarrow D^{-1}\exp(X_{\beta}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}X_{\beta}^{\top})X_{\beta}W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To generalize our result to multi-layer transformer architectures, we also need to efficiently approximate the gradients of the attention computation with respect to these weight matrices. We first define the attention computation loss function as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Attention loss)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the weights where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the input <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the attention loss as:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}}L(X,Y):=\min_{X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}}\|D(X)^{-1}\exp(X_{\ell}XX_{\ell}^{\top})X_{\ell}Y-B\|_{F}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}}L(X,Y):=\min_{X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}}\|D(X)^{-1}\exp(X_{\ell}XX_{\ell}^{\top})X_{\ell}Y-B\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the diagonal matrix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(X):=\diag(\exp(X_{\ell}XX_{\ell}^{\top}){\bf 1}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(X):=\diag(\exp(X_{\ell}XX_{\ell}^{\top}){\bf 1}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since the dependence of the attention loss <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear, it is very straightforward to compute the gradient with respect to the value weight <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial L(X,Y)}{\partial Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L(X,Y)}{\partial Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, prior works such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> focus on the optimization of <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial L(X,Y)}{\partial X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L(X,Y)}{\partial X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Approximate attention loss gradient computation)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the attention loss <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition E.1 (Attention loss). ‣ Appendix E GENERALIZATION TO MULTI-LAYER TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>.
For all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the goal is to output a vector <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{g}-\frac{\partial L(X,Y)}{\partial\mathrm{vec}\left(X\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{g}-\frac{\partial L(X,Y)}{\partial\mathrm{vec}\left(X\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\mathrm{vec}\left(X\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\mathrm{vec}\left(X\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix, and <math id="A5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}\left(x\right):=VV^{\top}A\left(x\right)-VE^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}\left(x\right):=VV^{\top}A\left(x\right)-VE^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> show that the gradient of the attention can be expressed as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial x}=\mathrm{vec}\left(X_{\ell}\left(\mathcal{P}_{1}\left(x\right)-\mathcal{P}_{2}\left(x\right)\right)X_{\ell}^{\top}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial L}{\partial x}=\mathrm{vec}\left(X_{\ell}\left(\mathcal{P}_{1}\left(x\right)-\mathcal{P}_{2}\left(x\right)\right)X_{\ell}^{\top}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{1}\left(x\right)=A\left(x\right)\circ\mathcal{Q}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{1}\left(x\right)=A\left(x\right)\circ\mathcal{Q}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{2}\left(x\right):=A\left(x\right)\diag\left(r\left(x\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{2}\left(x\right):=A\left(x\right)\diag\left(r\left(x\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\left(x\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\left(x\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> being defined as <math id="A5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\left(x\right)_{i}:=\langle A\left(x\right)_{i,*},\mathcal{Q}\left(x\right)_{i,*}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\left(x\right)_{i}:=\langle A\left(x\right)_{i,*},\mathcal{Q}\left(x\right)_{i,*}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> note that similar to the inference, the dominating term of the time complexity for computing <math id="A5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}L}{\mathrm{d}x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}L}{\mathrm{d}x}</annotation></semantics></math> is still the terms related to <math id="A5.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by replacing <math id="A5.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> shows that <math id="A5.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}L}{\mathrm{d}x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}L}{\mathrm{d}x}</annotation></semantics></math> can be approximated in nearly linear time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, our method expresses <math id="A5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}\left(x\right)/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}\left(x\right)/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Divide: Design a valid support basis. ‣ 3.2 Single-Threshold Support Basis ‣ 3 TECHNIQUE OVERVIEW ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)). Entries of <math id="A5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(A^{\left(s\right)}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> are small, so we can use the same technique as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> to approximate it by <math id="A5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)/d\right)-{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sparse matrix, but the product with other dense matrices is dense. Thus, further computation may still require quadratic time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To address this issue, we use the approximate singular value decomposition from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>. We can approximate its best rank-<math id="A5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> low-rank approximation in <math id="A5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity time (Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem E.3 (Theorem 8.1 in []). ‣ Appendix E GENERALIZATION TO MULTI-LAYER TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>). Choosing <math id="A5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=n^{o(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=n^{o(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can approximate <math id="A5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}L}{\mathrm{d}x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}L}{\mathrm{d}x}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(L\right)}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> sparsity time, and by sub-Gaussianity, we can generalize our method to multi-layer attention.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 8.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an algorithm that, with failure probability <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/10</annotation></semantics></math>,
finds matrices <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,W\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,W\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> with orthonormal columns, and diagonal
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathbb{R}^{k\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathbb{R}^{k\times k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A-LDW^{\top}\|_{F}\leq(1+\varepsilon)\Delta_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A-LDW^{\top}\|_{F}\leq(1+\varepsilon)\Delta_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The algorithm runs in time</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathrm{nnz}(A))+\widetilde{O}(nk^{2}\varepsilon^{-4}+k^{3}\varepsilon^{-5})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>nnz</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathrm{nnz}(A))+\widetilde{O}(nk^{2}\varepsilon^{-4}+k^{3}\varepsilon^{-5}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have now completed the presentation of the proofs for our first result, which uses the single-threshold support basis to approximate the attention computation without relying on the bounded-entry assumption required in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. Instead, we introduce the sub-Gaussian assumption, which, to the best of our knowledge, is satisfied by all existing transformer architectures (see Appendix <a href="#A13" title="Appendix M QUERY AND KEY ENTRIES DISTRIBUTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">M</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To extend our theoretical results to settings where the sub-Gaussian assumption may not hold, we next present a framework based on multiple-threshold support basis decomposition. Unlike the single-threshold approach, this method does not require any distributional assumptions on the entries of <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. However, due to the lower bound established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> (see Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem A.7 (Lower bound, Theorem 4.6 of []). ‣ A.1.3 Background: Main Results of [] ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>)<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          Assuming <span id="footnote1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">SETH</span>, with <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=O(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=O(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> and the entries of <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> not bounded above by <math id="footnote1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, no sub-quadratic time algorithm can approximate the attention computation to error <math id="footnote1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{a}=n^{-C_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{a}=n^{-C_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>, we must sacrifice the approximation error in order to achieve sub-quadratic runtime.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond the optimization perspective offered by our multiple-threshold support basis decomposition, we also establish a theoretical connection between polynomial attention and the Chebyshev polynomial approximation of softmax attention (Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 1.2 (The exact attention computation). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>). This provides a theoretical justification for the strong empirical performance of high-degree polynomial attention observed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our theoretical results go further than merely explaining existing empirical findings. Specifically, we show that the sum of multiple polynomial attentions achieves a significantly smaller <math id="A6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> error with respect to softmax attention, even though the <math id="A6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> error remains the same as that of a single polynomial approximation. This suggests that aggregating multiple polynomial approximations more accurately captures the behavior of softmax attention. We hope this insight will inspire future empirical research to investigate the benefits of summing multiple polynomial attentions, rather than relying solely on a single polynomial approximation as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In Appendix <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, we introduce some basic definitions for multiple thresholds support basis decomposition for decomposing the query <math id="A6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and key <math id="A6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> matrices. In Appendix <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Multi-Threshold Support Basis Decomposition of 𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤ ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, we prove that the decomposition satisfies the definition of support basis. In Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Additive Decomposition of exp(𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤/𝑑) ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, we use the mathematical property of the support basis developed earlier to get the additive decomposition of the <math id="A6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Basic Definitions</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we present the definitions for our multiple-threshold support basis decomposition. We aim to partition the query <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and key <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> matrices according to multiple value ranges, enabling a finer-grained approximation of the <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Multi-threshold decomposition of query and key matrices)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query and key matrices, respectively. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\}=T_{0}&lt;T_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;T_{m-1}&lt;T_{m}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\}=T_{0}&lt;T_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;T_{m-1}&lt;T_{m}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of thresholds.
For all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,*}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,*}&amp;\text{if }T_{\ell-1}\leq\max_{j\in[d]}|Q_{i,j}|&lt;T_{\ell}\\
{\bf 0}_{1\times d}&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,*}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,*}&amp;\text{if }T_{\ell-1}\leq\max_{j\in[d]}|Q_{i,j}|&lt;T_{\ell}\\
{\bf 0}_{1\times d}&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and similarly for <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now formally define how to decompose the matrix <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> into a sum of components based on multiple thresholds. By ensuring that the resulting matrices are disjoint, we preserve the additive structure necessary for efficient and accurate approximation. The following definition specifies the multi-threshold disjoint decomposition of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition F.2</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Multi-threshold disjoint decomposition of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query and key matrices, respectively. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\}=T_{0}&lt;T_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;T_{m-1}&lt;T_{m}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\}=T_{0}&lt;T_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;T_{m-1}&lt;T_{m}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of thresholds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)},K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)},K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition F.1 (Multi-threshold decomposition of query and key matrices). ‣ F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, and we define</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}:=Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}:=Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide an example to better illustrate the definitions above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example F.3</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(An example of 2-threshold disjoint decomposition of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive real number and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
c&amp;d\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>e</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
c&amp;d\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{3\times 2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;k\\
h&amp;j&amp;l\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{2\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>j</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>l</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;k\\
h&amp;j&amp;l\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{2\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|c|,|k|\geq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|c|,|k|\geq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the absolute value of other entries are smaller than <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This setup allows us to decompose the matrix product <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> into a sum of disjoint components based on the threshold values <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
c&amp;d\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;k\\
h&amp;j&amp;l\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>e</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>j</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>l</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
c&amp;d\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;k\\
h&amp;j&amp;l\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex136.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\begin{bmatrix}ag+bh&amp;ai+bj&amp;ak+bl\\
cg+dh&amp;ci+dj&amp;ck+dl\\
eg+hf&amp;ei+fj&amp;ek+fl\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\begin{bmatrix}ag+bh&amp;ai+bj&amp;ak+bl\\
cg+dh&amp;ci+dj&amp;ck+dl\\
eg+hf&amp;ei+fj&amp;ek+fl\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex137.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;ck+dl\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{2},T_{2}\right)}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
cg+dh&amp;ci+dj&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{2},T_{1}\right)}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;ak+bl\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;ek+fl\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{1},T_{2}\right)}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}ag+bh&amp;ai+bj&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
eg+hf&amp;ei+fj&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;ck+dl\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{2},T_{2}\right)}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
cg+dh&amp;ci+dj&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{2},T_{1}\right)}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;ak+bl\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;ek+fl\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{1},T_{2}\right)}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}ag+bh&amp;ai+bj&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
eg+hf&amp;ei+fj&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{A^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
c&amp;d\\
0&amp;0\\
\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;k\\
0&amp;0&amp;l\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
c&amp;d\\
0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;0\\
h&amp;j&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
0&amp;0\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;k\\
0&amp;0&amp;l\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
0&amp;0\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;0\\
h&amp;j&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>l</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>j</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>e</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>k</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>l</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>e</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>j</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
c&amp;d\\
0&amp;0\\
\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;k\\
0&amp;0&amp;l\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0\\
c&amp;d\\
0&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;0\\
h&amp;j&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
0&amp;0\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;k\\
0&amp;0&amp;l\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}}+\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}a&amp;b\\
0&amp;0\\
e&amp;f\end{bmatrix}}_{Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}}\underbrace{\begin{bmatrix}g&amp;i&amp;0\\
h&amp;j&amp;0\end{bmatrix}}_{\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This example illustrates how the product <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> can be partitioned into disjoint matrix components, forming a support basis that enables structured approximation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Multi-Threshold Support Basis Decomposition of <math id="A6.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that the multi-threshold decomposition of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a valid support basis. This helps with applying polynomial approximations to each component individually.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.4</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query and key matrices, respectively. Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\}=T_{0}&lt;T_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;T_{m-1}&lt;T_{m}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\}=T_{0}&lt;T_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;T_{m-1}&lt;T_{m}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of thresholds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the collection <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\}_{T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\}_{T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a support basis (as defined in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Definition B.5 (Support basis). ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>) of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Definition B.5 (Support basis). ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, it suffices to show:</span></p>
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{l=1}^{m}\sum_{l^{\prime}=1}^{m}A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}=QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{l=1}^{m}\sum_{l^{\prime}=1}^{m}A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}=QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are disjoint matrices (see Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition B.1 (Disjoint matrices). ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 1.<span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition F.1 (Multi-threshold decomposition of query and key matrices). ‣ F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, we can see that</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\quad\text{and}\quad K=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\quad\text{and}\quad K=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle QK^{\top}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle QK^{\top}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex140.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex142.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2.<span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall from Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition B.1 (Disjoint matrices). ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we say <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are disjoint matrices if for all <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\times\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\times\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(A^{\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(A^{\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose we have <math id="A6.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex143.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex144.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}_{i,*}\left(K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}_{j,*}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}_{i,*}\left(K^{\left(T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}_{j,*}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\neq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≠</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\neq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex145.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that <math id="A6.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}_{i,*}=Q_{i,*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{l}\right)}_{i,*}=Q_{i,*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{l}\right)}_{j,*}=K_{j,*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{l}\right)}_{j,*}=K_{j,*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by Definition <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition F.1 (Multi-threshold decomposition of query and key matrices). ‣ F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, we can see that for all <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{T}_{l}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{T_{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{T}_{l}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{T_{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{T_{l^{\prime}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{T_{l^{\prime}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, both <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(\overline{T}_{l}\right)}_{i,*}={\bf 0}_{1\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(\overline{T}_{l}\right)}_{i,*}={\bf 0}_{1\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)}_{k,*}={\bf 0}_{1\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)}_{k,*}={\bf 0}_{1\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we can get for all <math id="A6.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\times\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\times\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}\setminus\{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(A^{\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(A^{\left(\overline{T}_{l},\overline{T}_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Additive Decomposition of <math id="A6.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the entry-wise exponential function to disjoint matrices allows us to express the exponential of their sum as the sum of their exponentials. We now generalize Fact <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact B.2. ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, originally stated for the single-threshold support basis, to the multi-threshold support basis setting as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.5</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition F.1 (Multi-threshold decomposition of query and key matrices). ‣ F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>.
Let <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition F.2 (Multi-threshold disjoint decomposition of 𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤). ‣ F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this lemma using mathematical induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base case (when <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A6.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex148.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}+Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}+K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}+Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}+K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex149.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(T_{1}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}+Q^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{2}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex150.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(A^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}+A^{\left(T_{2},T_{1}\right)}+A^{\left(T_{1},T_{2}\right)}+A^{\left(T_{2},T_{2}\right)}\right)/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(A^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}+A^{\left(T_{2},T_{1}\right)}+A^{\left(T_{1},T_{2}\right)}+A^{\left(T_{2},T_{2}\right)}\right)/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex151.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{2},T_{1}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{1},T_{2}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{2},T_{2}\right)}/d\right)-3\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{2},T_{1}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{1},T_{2}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{2},T_{2}\right)}/d\right)-3\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{2}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{2}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(2^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{2}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{2}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(2^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, the third step follows from the definition of <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fourth step follows from combining Lemma <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma F.4. ‣ F.2 Multi-Threshold Support Basis Decomposition of 𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤ ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a> and Fact <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact B.2. ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, and the last step follows from <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inductive case.<span id="A6.SS3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary positive integer greater than or equal to <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose for all <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[t]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex153.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(t^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(t^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we consider the case of <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex155.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t+1}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t+1}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t+1}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t+1}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex156.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}+\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(K^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right.\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}+\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)\left(K^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right.\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~+\left.\left.\left(Q^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}+\left(Q^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)\left(K^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~+\left.\left.\left(Q^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}+\left(Q^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)\left(K^{\left(T_{t+1}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex158.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)+A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{t+1}\right)}+\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)+\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}\right)\right)/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left(\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)+A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{t+1}\right)}+\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)+\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}\right)\right)/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex159"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex159.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{t+1}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{t+1}\right)}/d\right)+\exp\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~+\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}/d\right)-3\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~+\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}/d\right)-3\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A6.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, the third step follows from the definition of <math id="A6.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> (as defined in Definition <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition F.2 (Multi-threshold disjoint decomposition of 𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤). ‣ F.1 Basic Definitions ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>), and the fourth step follows from combining Lemma <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma F.4. ‣ F.2 Multi-Threshold Support Basis Decomposition of 𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤ ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a> and Fact <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact B.2. ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We note that by Lemma <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma F.4. ‣ F.2 Multi-Threshold Support Basis Decomposition of 𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤ ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a> and Fact <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact B.2. ‣ B.1 Disjoint Matrices and Their Properties ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)-\left(t-1\right)\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{t+1},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)-\left(t-1\right)\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}\right)-\left(t-1\right)\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{t}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{t+1}\right)}\right)-\left(t-1\right)\cdot{\bf 1}_{n\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining everything together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex163.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{t+1}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t+1}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(t^{2}-1+2\left(t-1\right)+3\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{t+1}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t+1}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(t^{2}-1+2\left(t-1\right)+3\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex164.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{t+1}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t+1}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(\left(t+1\right)^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{t+1}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{t+1}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(\left(t+1\right)^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have constructed a multiple-threshold support basis which can make the <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be expressed as a sum of the exponential of each matrix in this support basis, namely <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Lemma <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma F.5. ‣ F.3 Additive Decomposition of exp(𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤/𝑑) ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.5</span></a>). We eventually want to approximate the attention computation problem <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{-1}\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{-1}\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)V</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 1.2 (The exact attention computation). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> for details). Therefore, we have to find a bound for <math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> so that the total running time for approximating <math id="A7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> numbers of <math id="A7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{-1}\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}\right)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{-1}\left(\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}\right)V</annotation></semantics></math> can be upper bounded.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, in Appendix <a href="#A7.SS1" title="G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, we specify the values of the thresholds <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{T_{\ell}\right\}_{\ell\in[m]\cup\{0\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{T_{\ell}\right\}_{\ell\in[m]\cup\{0\}}</annotation></semantics></math> for our multiple-threshold support basis—motivated by Birge bucketing—so that <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> can eventually be bounded. In Appendix <a href="#A7.SS2" title="G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.2</span></a>, we demonstrate how to tightly bound <math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A^{\circ p}-B^{\circ p}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A^{\circ p}-B^{\circ p}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> using the Mean Value Theorem. In Appendix <a href="#A7.SS3" title="G.3 Reducing the Softmax Attention Matrix to the Polynomial Attention Matrix ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>, we show that the <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix <math id="A7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 1.2 (The exact attention computation). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>) can be approximated by a sum of polynomial attention matrices (see Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem7" title="Definition G.7 (Polynomial attention matrix []). ‣ G.3 Reducing the Softmax Attention Matrix to the Polynomial Attention Matrix ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.7</span></a>) of the form <math id="A7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ p}</annotation></semantics></math>. In Appendix <a href="#A7.SS4" title="G.4 Reducing to Polynomial Attention Without Bucketing ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a>, we prove that the <math id="A7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> error between the <math id="A7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix and a single polynomial attention matrix is the same as that between the softmax matrix and the sum of polynomial attention matrices. Finally, in Appendix <a href="#A7.SS5" title="G.5 Bucketing Reduces the Error in ℓ_1 Norm ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.5</span></a>, we show that the <math id="A7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> error is significantly reduced when using Birge-bucketing-inspired thresholds.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Thresholds for Support Basis</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Birge bucketing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> is a well-known technique used in distribution testing: it partitions the support of a distribution into buckets to better analyze its tail behavior and test for heavy-tailedness. In particular, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> introduces an equal-weight bucketing scheme that partitions the domain of a distribution into intervals (or buckets) such that each bucket contains the same probability mass.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike the single-threshold support basis, which assumes that the entries of <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> are sub-Gaussian, the multiple-threshold support basis makes no specific distributional assumptions about the entries of <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. However, since their entries still follow some underlying distribution, we can apply the Birge bucketing technique to partition them. Because the exact distribution of the entries of <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is unknown<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            We even suppose that we do not have sample access to the entries of <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>, we cannot perform weight-based bucketing as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. Moreover, uniform bucketing—i.e., using a fixed bucket length of <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>—is also impractical, as the entries may take extremely large values, leading to an excessively large number of buckets <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we must approximate <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, a large value of <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> would prevent sub-quadratic runtime.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To keep <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> small, we define the thresholds as <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. We formally present the following definition:</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the bucketing parameter. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query and key matrices, respectively. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We define</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,*}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,*}&amp;\text{if }T_{\ell-1}\leq\max_{j\in[d]}|Q_{i,j}|&lt;T_{\ell}\\
{\bf 0}_{1\times d}&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,*}:=\begin{cases}Q_{i,*}&amp;\text{if }T_{\ell-1}\leq\max_{j\in[d]}|Q_{i,j}|&lt;T_{\ell}\\
{\bf 0}_{1\times d}&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and similarly for <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can eventually show that the number of buckets <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> can be bounded. It suffices to have <math id="A7.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> numbers of buckets.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact G.2</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the bucketing parameter. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query and key matrices, respectively. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex166"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M=\left\{m_{i}\mid[b,B]\subseteq\bigcup_{\ell=0}^{m_{i}-1}[T_{\ell},T_{\ell+1})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M=\left\{m_{i}\mid[b,B]\subseteq\bigcup_{\ell=0}^{m_{i}-1}[T_{\ell},T_{\ell+1})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be a sequence of positive integers.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{i}M=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{i}M=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We note that <math id="A7.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{\ell=0}^{m-1}[T_{\ell},T_{\ell+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{\ell=0}^{m-1}[T_{\ell},T_{\ell+1})</annotation></semantics></math> is an interval and, by definition, <math id="A7.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{0}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{0}=b</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it suffices to find the smallest <math id="A7.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{m}&gt;B." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{m}&gt;B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{m}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{m}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex169.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex170.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;B/b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;B/b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex171.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the smallest possible <math id="A7.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A7.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We need to ensure that within each bucket <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can make <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Although <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, without imposing any assumption, they can be much larger than <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we take out a large constant <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> to make <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we show that <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\geq\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\geq\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the bucketing parameter.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.3</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Normalized block decomposition)<span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the bucketing parameter.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\geq\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\geq\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma F.5. ‣ F.3 Additive Decomposition of exp(𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤/𝑑) ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.5</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(\ell\right)},K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(\ell\right)},K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot\underbrace{Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}}_{:=A^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot\underbrace{Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}}_{:=A^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A7.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have for all <math id="A7.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{p,q}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{p,q}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex174.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{q,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{q,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, we notice that <math id="A7.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|K^{\left(T_{\ell}^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|K^{\left(T_{\ell}^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By letting <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=\frac{b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}}{\sqrt{\log n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=\frac{b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}}{\sqrt{\log n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Additionally, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{p,q}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{p,q}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex176.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{q,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)_{q,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex177.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)_{q,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)_{q,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex178.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)_{q,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\sum_{k=1}^{d}\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\right)_{p,k}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)_{q,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex179.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Defining <math id="A7.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}:=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}:=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex180.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}}{\sqrt{\log n}}\frac{b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}}{\sqrt{\log n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}}{\sqrt{\log n}}\frac{b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}}{\sqrt{\log n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex181.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Basic Facts</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we use the Mean Value Theorem to show that for any arbitrary matrices <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B</annotation></semantics></math>, positive integers <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|A\right\|_{\infty},\left\|B\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|A\right\|_{\infty},\left\|B\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|A^{\circ p}-B^{\circ p}\right\|_{\infty}\leq p\cdot\beta^{p-1}\cdot\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|A^{\circ p}-B^{\circ p}\right\|_{\infty}\leq p\cdot\beta^{p-1}\cdot\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact G.4</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:=\max\left\{\left\|A\right\|_{\infty},\left\|B\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:=\max\left\{\left\|A\right\|_{\infty},\left\|B\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|A-B\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|A-B\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|A^{\circ p}-B^{\circ p}\right\|_{\infty}\leq p\cdot\beta^{p-1}\cdot\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|A^{\circ p}-B^{\circ p}\right\|_{\infty}\leq p\cdot\beta^{p-1}\cdot\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(x\right)=x^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(x\right)=x^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is differentiable on <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a point <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(a\right)-f\left(b\right)=f^{\prime}\left(c\right)\left(a-b\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(a\right)-f\left(b\right)=f^{\prime}\left(c\right)\left(a-b\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}\left(x\right)=px^{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}\left(x\right)=px^{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{p}-b^{p}=pc^{p-1}\left(a-b\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{p}-b^{p}=pc^{p-1}\left(a-b\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking absolute values on both sides gives:</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a^{p}-b^{p}|=|pc^{p-1}||a-b|=p|c|^{p-1}|a-b|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a^{p}-b^{p}|=|pc^{p-1}||a-b|=p|c|^{p-1}|a-b|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|c|\leq\max\left\{|a|,|b|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|c|\leq\max\left\{|a|,|b|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|a^{p}-b^{p}|\leq p\cdot\max\left\{|a|,|b|\right\}^{p-1}\cdot|a-b|&lt;p\cdot\max\left\{|a|,|b|\right\}^{p-1}\cdot\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|a^{p}-b^{p}|\leq p\cdot\max\left\{|a|,|b|\right\}^{p-1}\cdot|a-b|&lt;p\cdot\max\left\{|a|,|b|\right\}^{p-1}\cdot\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark G.5</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">By Lemma <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma F.5. ‣ F.3 Additive Decomposition of exp(𝑄⁢𝐾^⊤/𝑑) ‣ Appendix F MULTIPLE THRESHOLDS SUPPORT BASIS DECOMPOSITION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.5</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)-\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With some abuse of notation, we may say</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This does not affect the correctness and running time of our algorithm. We note that since the collection <math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\}_{T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A^{\left(T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\right)}\}_{T_{l},T_{l^{\prime}}\in\{T_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a support basis (as defined in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Definition B.5 (Support basis). ‣ B.2 Support Basis ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>) of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> transforms the zero entries to <math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Subtracting <math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(m^{2}-1\right)\cdot\mathbf{1}_{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to say that we redefine “<math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>” to “<math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>” in <math id="A7.Thmtheorem5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We have shown that <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=C^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma G.3 (Normalized block decomposition). ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>. Since in this paper, we apply <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(A)</annotation></semantics></math> entry-wisely to a matrix, we can get for all <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(cA)=\exp(A)^{\circ c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(cA)=\exp(A)^{\circ c}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact G.6</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1.</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2.</span><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and for all </span><math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\log n\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\log n\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 1.<span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex191.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex192.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex193"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex193.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Remark <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem5" title="Remark G.5. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.5</span></a>, the second step follows from the lemma statement, and the last step follows from <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(cA)=\exp(A)^{\circ c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(cA)=\exp(A)^{\circ c}</annotation></semantics></math> with the degree <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is applied entry-wisely to the matrix <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2.<span id="A7.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar as Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 (Bounded entry, an improved version of Lemma 3.3 in []). ‣ B.3 Bounded Entry ‣ Appendix B (BATCH) GAUSSIAN KERNEL DENSITY ESTIMATION VIA SINGLE THRESHOLD SUPPORT BASIS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, for any arbitrary <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex194.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex195.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|\sum_{l=1}^{d}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}_{i,l}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}_{j,l}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]}\left|\sum_{l=1}^{d}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}_{i,l}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}_{j,l}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex196.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}\left|\max_{i\in[n]}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\left|\max_{j\in[n]}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}_{j,l}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}\left|\max_{i\in[n]}Q^{\left(\ell\right)}_{i,l}\right|\cdot\left|\max_{j\in[n]}K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}_{j,l}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex197.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{l=1}^{d}o\left(\sqrt{\log n}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex198.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~o\left(d\log n\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~o\left(d\log n\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of the <math id="A7.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, the third step follows from the triangle inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), and the fourth step follows from Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma G.3 (Normalized block decomposition). ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Reducing the Softmax Attention Matrix to the Polynomial Attention Matrix</h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the polynomial attention matrix, which replaces the exponential in the standard attention formula with a polynomial of a given degree.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition G.7</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Polynomial attention matrix <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>)<span id="A7.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary positive integer. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The polynomial attention matrix <math id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="A7.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=\left(QK^{\top}\right)^{\circ p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=\left(QK^{\top}\right)^{\circ p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we show that the <math id="A7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix (see Definition <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 1.1 ((𝑄,𝐾)-softmax-attention matrix). ‣ 1.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>) is “close” to the sum of polynomial attention matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.8</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}\leq O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}\leq O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <span id="A7.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact G.6. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.6</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, since for all <math id="A7.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)\in[m]\times[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\log n\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\log n\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (see <span id="A7.SS3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact G.6. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.6</span></a>), we can construct <math id="A7.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon_{0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem3" title="Fact J.3. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.3</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex201.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex202"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex202.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\beta^{C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}-1}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\beta^{C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}-1}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem4" title="Fact G.4. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a> with</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex203"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta=\max\left\{\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty},\left\|U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta=\max\left\{\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty},\left\|U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering <math id="A7.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex204"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}}C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}}C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex204.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex205"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex205.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{2m}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{2m}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex206"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex206.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{B^{2}}{\log n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first and the second step follows from the fact that <math id="A7.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing (see from the lemma statement), the third step follows from <math id="A7.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering <math id="A7.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, by Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem4" title="Fact G.4. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex207"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex207.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max\left\{\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty},\left\|U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max\left\{\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty},\left\|U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex208"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex208.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty}+\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty}+\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex209"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex209.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\right)+\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left\|Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\right)+\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex210"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex210.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(o\left(\log n\right)\right)+\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(o\left(\log n\right)\right)+\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex211.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~n^{o(1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~n^{o(1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem4" title="Fact G.4. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a>, the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A7.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ G.3 Reducing the Softmax Attention Matrix to the Polynomial Attention Matrix ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), and the fourth step follows from <span id="A7.SS3.p7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact G.6. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.6</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining everything together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex212"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex213"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex213.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}n^{\frac{o(1)\cdot B^{2}}{\log n}}\epsilon_{0}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}n^{\frac{o(1)\cdot B^{2}}{\log n}}\epsilon_{0}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Reducing to Polynomial Attention Without Bucketing</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we note that the bucketing technique does not improve the <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-closeness between the polynomial attention matrix and the <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax attention matrix. Without using this bucketing technique, we obtain only a single polynomial attention matrix, which is precisely the case studied in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.9</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math> and by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)},U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)},U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex214"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}\leq O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}\leq O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This proof is similar to that of Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma G.8. ‣ G.3 Reducing the Softmax Attention Matrix to the Polynomial Attention Matrix ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.8</span></a>. By <span id="A7.SS4.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact G.6. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.6</span></a>, with <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex215"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex216"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex216.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{1+1}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{1+1}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex217"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex217.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{2m}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{2m}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex218"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex218.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~B^{2}/\log n," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~B^{2}/\log n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second step follows from <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, since we have <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\log n\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\leq o\left(\log n\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (see <span id="A7.SS4.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact G.6. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.6</span></a>), we can construct <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)},U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)},U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon_{0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}&lt;\epsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex219"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex220"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex220.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}\beta^{C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}-1}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}\beta^{C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}-1}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex221"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex221.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}\beta^{C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}-1}\epsilon_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}\beta^{C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}-1}\epsilon_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem4" title="Fact G.4. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a> and the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A7.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ G.4 Reducing to Polynomial Attention Without Bucketing ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering <math id="A7.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex222"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex222.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max\left\{\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty},\left\|U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max\left\{\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty},\left\|U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex223"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex223.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty}+\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)\right\|_{\infty}+\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex224"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex224.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left\|Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\right)+\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(\left\|Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right\|_{\infty}\right)+\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex225"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex225.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(o\left(\log n\right)\right)+\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(o\left(\log n\right)\right)+\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex226"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex226.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~n^{o(1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~n^{o(1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem4" title="Fact G.4. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.4</span></a>, the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A7.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ G.4 Reducing to Polynomial Attention Without Bucketing ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), and the fourth step follows from <span id="A7.SS4.p5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact G.6. ‣ G.2 Basic Facts ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.6</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining everything together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex227"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}\leq O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}n^{\frac{o(1)\cdot B^{2}}{\log n}}\epsilon_{0}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(1\right)}\left(K^{\left(1\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(1,1\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(1,1\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{1},T_{1}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}\leq O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}n^{\frac{o(1)\cdot B^{2}}{\log n}}\epsilon_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.5 </span>Bucketing Reduces the Error in <math id="A7.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> Norm</h3>

<div id="A7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following lemma, we analyze how the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> error between the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(Q,K\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(Q,K\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-softmax-attention matrix and its polynomial approximation is affected by the bucketing technique. While prior sections mainly focus on <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> approximations, the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm offers a complementary view by aggregating errors across entries. We show that the sum of multiple polynomial attention matrices generated by the bucketing technique significantly reduces the <math id="A7.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> error, thereby providing a stronger global approximation guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we analyze the case where we use the bucketing technique.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.10</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem10.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex228"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex229"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex229.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{n^{2}\epsilon_{0}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}}{\log\left(n\right)\log\left({\epsilon}+1\right)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{n^{2}\epsilon_{0}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}}{\log\left(n\right)\log\left({\epsilon}+1\right)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we consider the <math id="A7.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> error. We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex230"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
