<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{e^{B^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2}}}{c^{2}\log^{2}(n)\log^{2}(\epsilon+1)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{e^{B^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2}}}{c^{2}\log^{2}(n)\log^{2}(\epsilon+1)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A7.Ex240" title="In Proof. ‣ G.5 Bucketing Reduces the Error in ℓ_1 Norm ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), the third step follows from <span id="A7.SS5.p7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem4" title="Fact J.4 (Integral analysis). ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.4</span></a>, and the last step follows from the fact that <math id="A7.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2m+2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2m+2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the dominating term in numerator.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A7.Ex237" title="In Proof. ‣ G.5 Bucketing Reduces the Error in ℓ_1 Norm ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A7.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ G.5 Bucketing Reduces the Error in ℓ_1 Norm ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A7.Ex242" title="In Proof. ‣ G.5 Bucketing Reduces the Error in ℓ_1 Norm ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex245"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex246"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex246.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{n^{2}\epsilon_{0}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}}{\log\left(n\right)\log\left({\epsilon}+1\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{n^{2}\epsilon_{0}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}}{\log\left(n\right)\log\left({\epsilon}+1\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we analyze the case where we do not use the bucketing technique.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.11</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex247"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}=B^{2}/\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}=B^{2}/\log n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)},U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)},U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem11.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex248"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{1}\leq O\left(\frac{n^{2}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{1}\leq O\left(\frac{n^{2}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex249"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex250"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex250.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)_{i,j}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}^{C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)_{i,j}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,j}^{C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex251"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex251.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex252"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex252.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{n^{2}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{n^{2}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A7.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm and the second step follows from Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma G.9. ‣ G.4 Reducing to Polynomial Attention Without Bucketing ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.9</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.6 </span>Bucketing Reduces the Error in <math id="A7.SS6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> Norm</h3>

<div id="A7.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.12</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\left\lfloor\log_{1+\epsilon}\left(B/b\right)\right\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=\frac{b^{2}\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}}{\log n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)},U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can get a tighter bound for</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem12.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">compared with</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we consider the <math id="A7.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> error.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <span id="A7.SS6.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem9" title="Fact J.9. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.9</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex255"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex255.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Below, we apply the same multi-threshold support basis for <math id="A7.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, but for each matrix, we take out the constant <math id="A7.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> to simulate the case where we do not use bucketing.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex256"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex257.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex258.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right)\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left(\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right)\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex259.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the distributive law and the third step follows from <span id="A7.SS6.p4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem9" title="Fact J.9. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <span id="A7.SS6.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> and <span id="A7.SS6.p5.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 3</span> of Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem9" title="Fact J.9. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.9</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex260"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|A^{\circ k}+B^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|A^{\circ k}+B^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex260.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\left(A+B\right)^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}\leq\left\|A+B\right\|_{p}^{pk}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\left(A+B\right)^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}\leq\left\|A+B\right\|_{p}^{pk},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and for each <math id="A7.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can use it to show:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx126" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex261"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex262"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex262.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right\|_{p}^{p\cdot C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right\|_{p}^{p\cdot C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is tighter compared with</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx127" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex263"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex264"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex264.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right\|_{p}^{p\cdot C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(\ell,\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)\right\|_{p}^{p\cdot C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS6.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we analyze the case where we do not use the bucketing technique.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.13</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,m,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,m,d</annotation></semantics></math> be positive integers. Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\sum_{\ell=1}^{m}Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}=1}^{m}K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in Definition <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition G.1. ‣ G.1 Thresholds for Support Basis ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a>, with <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\min_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\max_{i\in[n],j\in[d]}\left\{|Q_{i,j}|,|K_{i,j}|\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for all <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[m]\cup\left\{0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ell}=b\left(1+\epsilon\right)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}=Q^{\left(T_{\ell}\right)}\left(K^{\left(T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\right)^{\top}=C^{\left(T_{\ell},T_{\ell^{\prime}}\right)}\cdot Q^{\left(\ell\right)}\left(K^{\left(\ell^{\prime}\right)}\right)^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\max\left\{\left\|Q\right\|_{\infty},\left\|K\right\|_{\infty}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx128" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex265"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)=\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}=B^{2}/\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}=B^{2}/\log n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (An improved version of Lemma 3.4 in []). ‣ A.1.2 Background: Approximating the Attention Computation Assuming 𝑑=𝑂(log𝑛) and Bounded Entries ‣ A.1 Background: Technique Overview of the Polynomial Method ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, there exists <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)},U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)},U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\epsilon_{0},r\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(Q^{\left(m\right)}\left(K^{\left(m\right)}\right)^{\top}/d\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem13.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx129" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex266"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}\leq O\left(\frac{n^{2}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}\leq O\left(\frac{n^{2}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx130" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex267"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex268"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex268.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\supp\left(A\right)\right|\cdot\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\supp\left(A\right)\right|\cdot\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{\infty}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex269"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex269.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left|\supp\left(A\right)\right|\cdot O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)^{p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left|\supp\left(A\right)\right|\cdot O\left(\frac{B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS6.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A7.SS6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm and the second step follows from Lemma <a href="#A7.Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma G.9. ‣ G.4 Reducing to Polynomial Attention Without Bucketing ‣ Appendix G THRESHOLD VALUES SPECIFICATION AND INTERVAL-BASED FACTORIZATION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx131" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex270"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}\leq O\left(\frac{n^{2/p}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\exp\left(QK^{\top}/d\right)-\left(U_{1}^{\left(m,m\right)}\left(U_{2}^{\left(m,m\right)}\right)^{\top}\right)^{\circ C^{\left(T_{m},T_{m}\right)}}\right\|_{p}\leq O\left(\frac{n^{2/p}B^{2}}{\log n}e^{o\left(B^{2}\right)}\epsilon_{0}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS6.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS6.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>SKETCHING REDUCES THE TIME COMPLEXITY OF POLYNOMIAL ATTENTION</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We note that <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> only analyzes the Frobenius norm error of the sketching matrix. In this section, we find the <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> error guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Appendix <a href="#A8.SS1" title="H.1 Probabilistic Statement of Two Vector JL Moment Property ‣ Appendix H SKETCHING REDUCES THE TIME COMPLEXITY OF POLYNOMIAL ATTENTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.1</span></a>, we express the two-vector JL moment property from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> into the probabilistic statement. In Appendix <a href="#A8.SS2" title="H.2 Pointwise Approximation of Polynomial Kernel via Sketching ‣ Appendix H SKETCHING REDUCES THE TIME COMPLEXITY OF POLYNOMIAL ATTENTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.2</span></a>, we use the sketching technique to show that for each <math id="A8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>, the inner product of the sketched vectors <math id="A8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\right),\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right)\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\right),\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right)\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is close to the original un-sketched polynomial kernel <math id="A8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*},\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right\rangle^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*},\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right\rangle^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. In Appendix <a href="#A8.SS3" title="H.3 Union Bound to All Entries ‣ Appendix H SKETCHING REDUCES THE TIME COMPLEXITY OF POLYNOMIAL ATTENTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.3</span></a>, we use the union bound over all <math id="A8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> to show that the <math id="A8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm of <math id="A8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}\right)^{\circ p}-\phi^{\prime}(U_{1})\phi^{\prime}(U_{2})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(U_{1}U_{2}^{\top}\right)^{\circ p}-\phi^{\prime}(U_{1})\phi^{\prime}(U_{2})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded, where the randomized feature mapping <math id="A8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied row-wisely to matrices <math id="A8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Probabilistic Statement of Two Vector JL Moment Property</h3>

<div id="A8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formalize the guarantee provided by random projections. This guarantees approximately preserving the inner products between vectors with high probability. This result is a direct consequence of the JL moment property (Definition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem11" title="Definition A.11 (JL Moment Property, Definition 4.2 in []). ‣ A.2 Background: Sketching and Polynomial Attention ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>) and plays a crucial role in ensuring that geometric relationships between vectors are maintained under dimensionality reduction:</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma H.1</span></span><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Inner Product Preservation)<span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random matrix satisfying the <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\delta,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\delta,t)</annotation></semantics></math>-JL moment property for some <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon,\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon,\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and integer <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any vectors <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex271" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|\leq\epsilon\|x\|_{2}\|y\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|\leq\epsilon\|x\|_{2}\|y\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma A.12 (Two vector JL Moment Property, Lemma 4.1 in []). ‣ A.2 Background: Sketching and Polynomial Attention ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx132" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right\|_{L_{t}}\leq\epsilon\delta^{1/t}\|x\|_{2}\|y\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right\|_{L_{t}}\leq\epsilon\delta^{1/t}\|x\|_{2}\|y\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem11" title="Definition A.11 (JL Moment Property, Definition 4.2 in []). ‣ A.2 Background: Sketching and Polynomial Attention ‣ Appendix A PRELIMINARIES ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx133" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right\|_{L_{t}}=\E\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}\right]^{1/t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Sx</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Sy</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right\|_{L_{t}}=\E\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}\right]^{1/t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A8.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ H.1 Probabilistic Statement of Two Vector JL Moment Property ‣ Appendix H SKETCHING REDUCES THE TIME COMPLEXITY OF POLYNOMIAL ATTENTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A8.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ H.1 Probabilistic Statement of Two Vector JL Moment Property ‣ Appendix H SKETCHING REDUCES THE TIME COMPLEXITY OF POLYNOMIAL ATTENTION ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx134" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex272"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}\right]\leq\epsilon^{t}\delta\|x\|_{2}^{t}\|y\|_{2}^{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Sx</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Sy</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}\right]\leq\epsilon^{t}\delta\|x\|_{2}^{t}\|y\|_{2}^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Markov’s inequality (see Fact <a href="#A10.Thmtheorem7" title="Fact J.7 (Markov’s Inequality). ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">J.7</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx135" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex273"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex273.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|&gt;\epsilon\|x\|_{2}\|y\|_{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|&gt;\epsilon\|x\|_{2}\|y\|_{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex273.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}&gt;\epsilon^{t}\|x\|_{2}^{t}\|y\|_{2}^{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>y</mi><msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}&gt;\epsilon^{t}\|x\|_{2}^{t}\|y\|_{2}^{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex274"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex274.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}\right]}{\epsilon^{t}\|x\|_{2}^{t}\|y\|_{2}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{\mathbb{E}\left[\left|(Sx)^{\top}(Sy)-x^{\top}y\right|^{t}\right]}{\epsilon^{t}\|x\|_{2}^{t}\|y\|_{2}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.Ex275"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex275.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex275.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Pointwise Approximation of Polynomial Kernel via Sketching</h3>

<div id="A8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we show that the randomized feature mapping <math id="A8.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can approximate the value of a degree-<math id="A8.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> polynomial kernel between any pair of vectors up to a small additive error, with high probability:</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma H.2</span></span><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pointwise Approximation of Polynomial Kernel via Sketching)<span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\}_{i=1}^{n},\{\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\}_{j=1}^{n}\subset\mathbb{R}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\}_{i=1}^{n},\{\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\}_{j=1}^{n}\subset\mathbb{R}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> be an even positive integer.
Let <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> be the accuracy parameter and <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> be the failure probability.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, there exists a randomized feature mapping</span></p>
<table id="A8.Ex276" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex276.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}:\mathbb{R}^{r}\to\mathbb{R}^{z^{2}},\quad\text{for }z=\Theta\left(p\epsilon^{-2}\log(1/\delta)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}:\mathbb{R}^{r}\to\mathbb{R}^{z^{2}},\quad\text{for }z=\Theta\left(p\epsilon^{-2}\log(1/\delta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">defined as <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}(x):=\left(Sx^{\otimes\left(p/2\right)}\right)^{\otimes 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}(x):=\left(Sx^{\otimes\left(p/2\right)}\right)^{\otimes 2}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in\mathbb{R}^{z\times r^{p/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in\mathbb{R}^{z\times r^{p/2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sketching matrix, such that for all <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, the following hold with probability at least <math id="A8.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx136" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.Ex277"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.Ex277.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\left\langle\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\right),\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right)\right\rangle-\left\langle\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*},\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right\rangle^{p}\right|\leq\epsilon\|\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\|_{2}^{p}\|\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\|_{2}^{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\left\langle\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\right),\phi^{\prime}\left(\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right)\right\rangle-\left\langle\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*},\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\right\rangle^{p}\right|\leq\epsilon\|\left(U_{1}\right)_{i,*}\|_{2}^{p}\|\left(U_{2}\right)_{j,*}\|_{2}^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
