<div id="A10.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2.<span id="A10.p21.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we consider</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx215" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex410"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex410.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{1}^{m+1}\frac{b^{2}(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}}}{c\log^{2}(n)\log(\epsilon+1)}\,\mathrm{d}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{1}^{m+1}\frac{b^{2}(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}}}{c\log^{2}(n)\log(\epsilon+1)}\,\mathrm{d}y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use <math id="A10.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>-substitution by defining <math id="A10.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx216" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex411"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex411.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}y=\frac{1}{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}\log(\epsilon+1)}\mathrm{d}u." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}y=\frac{1}{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}\log(\epsilon+1)}\mathrm{d}u.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx217" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex412"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex412.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\int_{1}^{m+1}\frac{b^{2}(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}}}{c\log^{2}(n)\log(\epsilon+1)}\,\mathrm{d}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\int_{1}^{m+1}\frac{b^{2}(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}}}{c\log^{2}(n)\log(\epsilon+1)}\,\mathrm{d}y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex413"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex413.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex413.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{c\log^{2}(n)\log(\epsilon+1)}\int_{1}^{m+1}b^{2}(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}}\,\mathrm{d}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{c\log^{2}(n)\log(\epsilon+1)}\int_{1}^{m+1}b^{2}(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{y+m+1}}\,\mathrm{d}y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex414"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex414.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex414.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{c^{2}\log^{2}(n)\log^{2}(\epsilon+1)}\int_{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{m+2}}^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2m+2}}e^{u}\,\mathrm{d}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{c^{2}\log^{2}(n)\log^{2}(\epsilon+1)}\int_{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{m+2}}^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2m+2}}e^{u}\,\mathrm{d}u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex415"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex415.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex415.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2m+2}}-e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{m+2}}}{c^{2}\log^{2}(n)\log^{2}(\epsilon+1)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{2m+2}}-e^{b^{2}c(\epsilon+1)^{m+2}}}{c^{2}\log^{2}(n)\log^{2}(\epsilon+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p24.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p24.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact J.5</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Multiplicative Chernoff Bound)<span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent random variables taking values in <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="A10.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx218" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex416"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex416.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex416.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }0&lt;\delta\leq 1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }0&lt;\delta\leq 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex417"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex417.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex417.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }\delta&gt;1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }\delta&gt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact J.6</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary positive integer.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<ul id="A10.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A10.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1.</span><span id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A10.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle a^{\otimes 2},b^{\otimes 2}\rangle=\langle a,b\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle a^{\otimes 2},b^{\otimes 2}\rangle=\langle a,b\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2.</span><span id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A10.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle a^{\otimes p},b^{\otimes p}\rangle=\langle a,b\rangle^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle a^{\otimes p},b^{\otimes p}\rangle=\langle a,b\rangle^{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (generalizing </span><span id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span><span id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to arbitrary </span><math id="A10.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 3.</span><span id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A10.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a^{\otimes p}\|_{2}=\|a\|_{2}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a^{\otimes p}\|_{2}=\|a\|_{2}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 1.<span id="A10.p25.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx219" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex418"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex418.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes 2},b^{\otimes 2}\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes 2},b^{\otimes 2}\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex418.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle a\otimes a,b\otimes b\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle a\otimes a,b\otimes b\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex419"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex419.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex419.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}(a_{i}a_{j})(b_{i}b_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}(a_{i}a_{j})(b_{i}b_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex420"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex420.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex420.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}a_{i}b_{i}a_{j}b_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}a_{i}b_{i}a_{j}b_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex421"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex421.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex421.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}a_{i}b_{i}\right)\left(\sum_{j=1}^{d}a_{j}b_{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}a_{i}b_{i}\right)\left(\sum_{j=1}^{d}a_{j}b_{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex422"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex422.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex422.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}a_{i}b_{i}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}a_{i}b_{i}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex423"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex423.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex423.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle a,b\rangle^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle a,b\rangle^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p26.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p26.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A10.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\otimes 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\otimes 2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\otimes 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\otimes 2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second step follows from the definition of inner product and Kronecker product, the third step follows from the associative law of multiplication, and the last step follows from the definition of inner product.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2<span id="A10.p27.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this part using mathematical induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">We treat <span id="A10.p29.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> as the base case, and below, we prove the inductive case.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume for any given positive integer <math id="A10.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx220" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes k},b^{\otimes k}\rangle=\langle a,b\rangle^{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes k},b^{\otimes k}\rangle=\langle a,b\rangle^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similar as what we have in <span id="A10.p31.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx221" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex424"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex424.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes(k+1)},b^{\otimes(k+1)}\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes(k+1)},b^{\otimes(k+1)}\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex424.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle a^{\otimes k}\otimes a,b^{\otimes k}\otimes b\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle a^{\otimes k}\otimes a,b^{\otimes k}\otimes b\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex425"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex425.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex425.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{d}\sum_{i=1}^{d^{k}}\left(\left(a^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}a_{j}\right)\left(\left(b^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}b_{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{d}\sum_{i=1}^{d^{k}}\left(\left(a^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}a_{j}\right)\left(\left(b^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}b_{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex426"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex426.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex426.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{d}\sum_{i=1}^{d^{k}}\left(a^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}a_{j}\left(b^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}b_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{j=1}^{d}\sum_{i=1}^{d^{k}}\left(a^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}a_{j}\left(b^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}b_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex427"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex427.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex427.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d^{k}}\left(a^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}\left(b^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}\right)\left(\sum_{j=1}^{d}a_{j}b_{j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d^{k}}\left(a^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}\left(b^{\otimes k}\right)_{i}\right)\left(\sum_{j=1}^{d}a_{j}b_{j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex428"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex428.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex428.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle a^{\otimes k},b^{\otimes k}\rangle\cdot\langle a,b\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle a^{\otimes k},b^{\otimes k}\rangle\cdot\langle a,b\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p31.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p31.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A10.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\otimes(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\otimes(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\otimes(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\otimes(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second step follows from the definition of inner product and Kronecker product, the third step follows from the associative law of multiplication, and the last step follows from the definition of inner product.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the inductive hypothesis (Eq. (<a href="#A10.E57" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>)), we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx222" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex429"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex429.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes(k+1)},b^{\otimes(k+1)}\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle a^{\otimes(k+1)},b^{\otimes(k+1)}\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex429.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle a,b\rangle^{k}\cdot\langle a,b\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle a,b\rangle^{k}\cdot\langle a,b\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex430"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex430.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex430.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle a,b\rangle^{k+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle a,b\rangle^{k+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 3.<span id="A10.p33.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can get</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx223" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex431"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex431.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|a^{\otimes p}\|_{2}^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|a^{\otimes p}\|_{2}^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex431.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i_{1}=1}^{d}\cdots\sum_{i_{p}=1}^{d}(a_{i_{1}}a_{i_{2}}\cdots a_{i_{p}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i_{1}=1}^{d}\cdots\sum_{i_{p}=1}^{d}(a_{i_{1}}a_{i_{2}}\cdots a_{i_{p}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex432"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex432.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex432.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i_{1}=1}^{d}\cdots\sum_{i_{p}=1}^{d}a_{i_{1}}^{2}a_{i_{2}}^{2}\cdots a_{i_{p}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i_{1}=1}^{d}\cdots\sum_{i_{p}=1}^{d}a_{i_{1}}^{2}a_{i_{2}}^{2}\cdots a_{i_{p}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex433"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex433.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex433.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}a_{i}^{2}\right)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d}a_{i}^{2}\right)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex434"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex434.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex434.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\|a\|_{2}^{2p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\|a\|_{2}^{2p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p34.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p34.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of the <math id="A10.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm and the Kronecker product, and the last step follows from the definition of the <math id="A10.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking square roots of both sides, we have</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex435" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex435.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a^{\otimes p}\|_{2}=\|a\|_{2}^{p}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a^{\otimes p}\|_{2}=\|a\|_{2}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p35.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p35.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact J.7</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Markov’s Inequality)<span id="A10.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a non-negative random variable and let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex436" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex436.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[X\geq a]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}[X]}{a}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X\geq a]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}[X]}{a}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact J.8</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Union Bound)<span id="A10.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},A_{2},\dots,A_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},A_{2},\dots,A_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be events in a probability space. Then</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex437" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex437.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\left[\bigcup_{i=1}^{n}A_{i}\right]\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Pr[A_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[\bigcup_{i=1}^{n}A_{i}\right]\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Pr[A_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact J.9</span></span><span id="A10.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be disjoint matrices. Let <math id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> be arbitrary positive integers.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.Thmtheorem9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can get</span></p>
<ul id="A10.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A10.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1.</span><span id="A10.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A10.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(A+B\right)^{\circ p}=\left(A\right)^{\circ p}+\left(B\right)^{\circ p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(A+B\right)^{\circ p}=\left(A\right)^{\circ p}+\left(B\right)^{\circ p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span><span id="A10.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A10.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|A+B\right\|_{p}^{p}=\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{p}+\left\|B\right\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|A+B\right\|_{p}^{p}=\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{p}+\left\|B\right\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A10.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A10.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 3</span><span id="A10.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="A10.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|A^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}\leq\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{pk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|A^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}\leq\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{pk}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A10.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 1.<span id="A10.p36.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p37" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A10.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint matrices, for any arbitrary <math id="A10.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(i,j\right)\in[n]\times[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can either have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx224" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{i,j}\neq 0\text{ and }B_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{i,j}\neq 0\text{ and }B_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p37.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p37.2.1" class="ltx_text">or</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx225" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{i,j}\neq 0\text{ and }A_{i,j}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{i,j}\neq 0\text{ and }A_{i,j}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">If Eq. (<a href="#A10.E58" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) holds, then we can get</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx226" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex438"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex438.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\left(A+B\right)^{\circ p}\right)_{i,j}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\left(A+B\right)^{\circ p}\right)_{i,j}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex438.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(A+B\right)_{i,j}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(A+B\right)_{i,j}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex439"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex439.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex439.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~A_{i,j}^{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~A_{i,j}^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p39" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p39.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p39.1.1" class="ltx_text">If Eq. (<a href="#A10.E59" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix J MORE FACTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) holds, then we can get</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx227" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex440"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex440.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\left(A+B\right)^{\circ p}\right)_{i,j}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\left(A+B\right)^{\circ p}\right)_{i,j}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex440.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(A+B\right)_{i,j}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(A+B\right)_{i,j}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex441"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex441.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex441.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~B_{i,j}^{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~B_{i,j}^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2.<span id="A10.p40.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p41" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p41.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p41.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can get</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx228" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex442"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex442.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|A+B\right\|_{p}^{p}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|A+B\right\|_{p}^{p}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex442.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A+B)_{i,j}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A+B)_{i,j}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex443"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex443.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex443.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A_{i,j}^{p}+B_{i,j}^{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A_{i,j}^{p}+B_{i,j}^{p})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex444"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex444.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex444.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}A_{i,j}^{p}+\sum_{i,j}B_{i,j}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}A_{i,j}^{p}+\sum_{i,j}B_{i,j}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex445"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex445.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex445.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{p}+\left\|B\right\|_{p}^{p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{p}+\left\|B\right\|_{p}^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p41.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p41.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A10.p41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> norm and the second step follows from <span id="A10.p41.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 3.<span id="A10.p42.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p43" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx229" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.Ex446"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex446.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|A^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|A^{\circ k}\right\|_{p}^{p}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex446.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A^{\circ k})_{i,j}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A^{\circ k})_{i,j}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex447"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex447.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex447.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A_{i,j}^{k})^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A_{i,j}^{k})^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex448"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex448.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex448.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A_{i,j}^{p})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i,j}(A_{i,j}^{p})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex449"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex449.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex449.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i,j}A_{i,j}^{p}\right)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\sum_{i,j}A_{i,j}^{p}\right)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.Ex450"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex450.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.Ex450.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{pk}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|A\right\|_{p}^{pk}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p43.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p43.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix K </span>EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS</h2>

<section id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computational Efficiency</h5>

<figure id="A11.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A11.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.01643v1/time.png" id="A11.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/179;" width="238" height="179" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Time vs Threshold</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A11.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.01643v1/kernel_err.png" id="A11.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/179;" width="238" height="179" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Error vs Threshold</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Runtime and accuracy comparison of attention approximation methods. Our single-threshold support-basis method achieves sub-quadratic efficiency as the threshold increases, eventually outperforming exact attention and matching the performance of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. Moreover, our method consistently yields lower relative Frobenius norm error compared with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>. Once the threshold becomes sufficiently large (around 0.4), all entries are approximated, and the error becomes comparable to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first compare the computational efficiency of the original Transformer, the method of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, and our proposed approach. We used an Apple M3 CPU to run this experiment.
Specifically, we set <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8192\times 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8192</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8192\times 64</annotation></semantics></math> matrices, corresponding to a sequence length of 8192 and a hidden dimension of 64—parameters consistent with real-world Transformer deployments.
To satisfy our sub-Gaussian assumption, each entry of <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn independently from a Gaussian distribution with mean <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and standard deviation <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A11.EGx230" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.Ex451"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.Ex451.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{i,j}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1^{2}),\quad K_{i,j}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1^{2}),\quad\forall(i,j)\in[8192]\times[64]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>0.1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>0.1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>8192</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{i,j}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1^{2}),\quad K_{i,j}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,0.1^{2}),\quad\forall(i,j)\in[8192]\times[64].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our method with thresholds ranging from 0.15 to 0.5.
Figure <a href="#A11.F4.sf1" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Computational Efficiency ‣ Appendix K EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4a</span></a> reports the runtime of the three methods. As the threshold increases, the runtime of our method decreases since fewer entries require exact computation.
Unlike <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, which applies approximation uniformly, our method involves both exact and approximate computations. Consequently, it runs slower than <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> at low thresholds.
However, once the threshold exceeds 0.26, the fraction of entries requiring exact computation becomes sufficiently small, and our method achieves faster runtime than exact attention. Figure <a href="#A11.F4.sf2" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Computational Efficiency ‣ Appendix K EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4b</span></a> presents the relative Frobenius error of the approximated attention matrix. Across all thresholds, our method consistently yields lower error than <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, with an appropriately chosen threshold (approximately <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in[0.26,0.35]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in[0.26,0.35]</annotation></semantics></math>), our approach achieves a superior trade-off between computational efficiency and approximation accuracy compared to existing baselines. Within this range, our method runs faster than exact attention computation (Figure <a href="#A11.F4.sf1" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Computational Efficiency ‣ Appendix K EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4a</span></a>) and yields strictly smaller errors than <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> (Figure <a href="#A11.F4.sf2" title="In Figure 4 ‣ Computational Efficiency ‣ Appendix K EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS ‣ Support Basis: Fast Attention Beyond Bounded Entries" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4b</span></a>). This reduction in error allows our method to achieve downstream task performance comparable to exact attention, whereas <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> attains <math id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\%</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy on these tasks, as shown below.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
